      "summary": "I rendered all 13 pages in headless Chrome and ran 7 more checks with ?view=team. On every page I collected each <a href>, clicked the in-page anchors in Chrome over the DevTools protocol, and curled every external URL and image. I did not edit any file.\n\nWhat passes:\n- The top nav is the same six links in the same order on all six proposal pages, and aria-current marks the right one on each.\n- All internal links resolve to existing files.\n- All 44 cross-page anchors exist after render and scroll to the right place. That covers roi.html#p01–p07, agents.html#play-01–07, all 16 agents.html#<agent-id>, million.html#idea-1–11 and research.html#ai, #competitors and #considered. research.html#doc-* deep links open the matching report panel.\n- Every same-page anchor has a target.\n- The ?view=team links really switch the page to team view.\n- Every prototype dock has 7 cards, marks the current one with aria-current, and its \"All prototypes\" link goes to ../index.html.\n- The mailto links are well formed and their subjects are encoded.\n- All 204 external links on the pages use https with target=_blank and rel=noopener.\n- Nothing links to 00-test.html, _check.html or FRAMEWORK.md.\n- All 147 images the pages request return 200, as do all 110 catalog image URLs and all local assets. No page requests anything that fails with 4xx.\n\nProblems found:\n- High: one source domain (citymatters.london) now serves a gambling spam site.\n- Medium: team view sticks after one visit; two relative links in the reports return 404; the prototype dock has no AI agents link; two agents.html evidence links are dead; the proposal has no contents navigation below 1024px.\n- Low: several smaller issues, listed below.",
