    {
      "lens": "numbers",
      "summary": "I checked the numbers on all 13 rendered pages (headless Chrome dumps) against assets/site-data.js, assets/catalog.js and research/cfo-review.md. No files were edited.\n\nWhat matches everywhere:\n- **Play figures.** Every play's year-1 mid/low/high, run-rate and margin is the CFO-corrected value and is identical on the hub cards, the roi.html bars, the proposal table and each prototype's drawer: P1 $341K ($171–568K), $726K, 40%; P2 $179K ($81–339K), $581K, 22%; P3 $322K ($169–484K), $612K, 30%; P4 $162K ($68–323K), $622K, 40%; P5 $95K ($50–232K), $315K, 38%; P6 $191K ($113–276K), $417K, 45%; P7 $129K ($46–271K), $308K, 20%. Each play's math text re-adds correctly.\n- **Five-play portfolio.** In-plan mids sum to $1,111K (year 1) and $2,692K (year 2). After 28% that is $800K / $1.94M, with gross profit $302K / $742K (38%). Hub, roi.html and proposal all agree.\n- **$1M path.** $315K + $726K + $622K = $1.663M, less 25% = $1.247M. The ramp ($389K → $1,514K) and the 11 idea scores (86/78/75/74/70/63/63/59/52/46/33) match the CFO tables.\n- **Other counts.** The fee ($3,500 a month + $6,000) matches on every page. 16 agents = 10 + 6. The agent cost range matches the sum of the cards ($1,565–$3,540). Research stats match (979/743, ~292, 4.8★/611, 30K, 6 routes, ~$2.5M).\n- **Prices.** Every per-meal and per-item price I spot-checked in the prototypes matches catalog.js. This covers the plan builder items, partner cases, At Work menu, gift levels, Club cut list and points, fundraiser packs and the coach week. I found no catalog price errors.\n\nWhat is inconsistent:\n- **Stale pre-CFO text in some plays.** Text fields that were not re-synced after the CFO pass still quote the old figures:\n  - Play 1: churn 9%/8.5% and 140/250/310 subscribers.\n  - Play 2: $260 average order, 0.85, -$18K/+$58K.\n  - Play 5: 40% margin, 25 accounts / 500 gifts, 0.85.\n  - Idea 7: 17% margin, $8K setup, five January pilots (Play 7 has four groups in December 2026).\n  - Idea 3: tiers $129/$229/$299.\n  - Agents page: Goal Plans 251, 15–25 staff.\n- **$1M path shown three ways.** The path card says $1.2M, the million intro and proposal §6 say \"$1.3M\", and the path builder on the same page says $1.6M / $626K.\n- **Calculator and range problems:**\n  - The hub/proposal ranges ($400K–$1.0M and $900K–$2.3M) are not low–high ranges; the top end is just the expected case plus 15%.\n  - Year-2 low/high are scaled from year-1 ratios instead of using each play's own year-2 range.\n  - roi.html costs every play at monthly × 12, so year-1 costs come out at $322K against the plays' own ~$285K. Year-2 costs come out at $278K against the plays' own ~$364K, so the headline shows 2.3x where the plays' own costs give 1.8x.\n- **Sample panels.** Two prototype sample panels disagree with their plays: the Gift Studio holiday counts and the Butcher Club P&L.\n- **Layout mismatch.** The million page's first-test list puts each test under the wrong idea.\n\nMost of the fixes are text replacements in /Users/erwingarcia/Claude/JWFOODSPROPOSAL/site/assets/site-data.js. The calculator fixes are in /Users/erwingarcia/Claude/JWFOODSPROPOSAL/site/million.html, /Users/erwingarcia/Claude/JWFOODSPROPOSAL/site/roi.html and /Users/erwingarcia/Claude/JWFOODSPROPOSAL/tools/build_data.py. Line numbers are given in each finding.",
      "findings": [
