          "where": "\"Why this makes money\" > KPIs and Assumptions tabs; roi.html P1 'Assumptions' list; proposal P1 'KPIs.' paragraph; team console KPI tile",
          "issue": "Play 1 still shows pre-CFO churn and subscriber counts that contradict its own math in the same drawer. The math says 10% churn in year 1 and 9% in year 2, avg 136 active, ~239 by Oct 2027 and ~299 avg in year 2. The KPIs say 'Active subscribers: 140 avg in year 1; 250 by Oct 2027; 310 avg in year 2' and 'Monthly churn: 9% or lower in year 1; 8.5% in year 2'. The Assumptions say 'Monthly churn is 9% in year 1 and 8.5% in year 2'. The team tile says 'Monthly churn 8.6% target 9% or lower'. The proposal's own risk table says 'Modelled at 10% monthly churn'. The CFO values (10%/9%, 136/239/299) are the right ones.",
          "fix": "site-data.js line 170: \"136 avg in year 1; ~239 by Oct 2027; ~299 avg in year 2\". Line 174: \"10% or lower in year 1; 9% in year 2\". Line 200: \"Monthly churn is 10% in year 1 and 9% in year 2 (Eightx: replenishment 5-8%, meal kits 8-15%).\" prototypes/01-goal-plan-builder.html line 1603: change 'target 9% or lower' to 'target 10% or lower'.",
