          "issue": "The whole site asks Bill to pick 3 or 4 prototypes, but there is no way to mark one. He has to open 7 prototypes on his phone, remember their names, scroll about 10 screens back down the hub and type an email from scratch. The mailto has a subject line only, with no body and no list. Nothing in any prototype lets him say \"I like this one\".",
          "evidence": "index.html:245 href=\"mailto:erwin.garcia@minastech.ca?subject=J%26W%20Foods%3A%20the%20prototypes%20to%20build%20first\" has no body. concept.js has no shortlist, pick or vote control (grep found none). The cards offer only Open, The math, Team view and AI agents.",
          "fix": "1) concept.js bar actions: add '<button type=\"button\" class=\"jwc-pill jwc-pick\" aria-pressed=\"false\">☆ Shortlist this</button>'. On click, toggle the play number n in localStorage key 'jw-picks' (a JSON array, wrapped in try/catch), set the label to '★ On my shortlist' and show JWC.toast('Added. Send your shortlist from the hub.'). 2) Hub cards: add the same toggle under each 'Open prototype' button. 3) Build the 'Your turn' link from the picks: 'mailto:...?subject=' + encodeURIComponent('J&W Foods: our shortlist') + '&body=' + encodeURIComponent('Our picks:\\n' + picks.map(n => '- ' + J.plays[n-1].name).join('\\n') + '\\n\\nNotes:'). Change the button text to 'Email our shortlist (' + picks.length + ') →'.",
          "severity": "high"
        },
        {
          "page": "index.html (hub) + roi.html + million.html",
          "where": "Hub intro ('a plan that starts with three'), the 'Your turn' card, the '$1M question' box; business case header; $1M 'short version'",
          "issue": "Bill cannot tell what plan he is being sold:\n- The hub says \"a plan that starts with three\" but never says which three, and the flagship 'start here' card is Goal Plans.\n- The $1M box says start the Corporate Gift Studio this month. On the hub it is card #5, with no badge.\n- The business case opens on a different '5 of 7 plays' plan (P1, P3, P4, P5, P6). The hub's $400K–$1.0M (central $800K) figure comes from that plan.\n- The hub's $1M box lists Gift Studio $315K, Goal Plans $726K and J&W at Work $622K with no label. The same plays' cards a few screens up say $95K, $341K and $162K 'in year one', so Bill sees two different numbers for each name.",
          "evidence": "Hub text: 'a plan that starts with three'; '$400K–$1.0M added revenue in year one... Central about $800K'; $1M box rows '$315K', '$726K', '$622K'. roi.html: '5 of 7 plays · expected case · 28% overlap removed' (checkboxes 1, 3, 4, 5, 6 checked). million: path = Gift Studio, Goal Plans, J&W at Work. index.html:270 renders money(idea.sales.mid) with no '/yr once running' label.",
          "fix": "Choose one recommended start and say it the same way everywhere.\n- Hero intro: replace '...and a plan that starts with three.' with '...We recommend starting with three: the Corporate Gift Studio now, Goal Plans in December and J&W at Work in January.'\n- Add a 'Recommended first' badge on cards 01, 04 and 05.\n- index.html:270: render money((idea.sales||{}).mid) + '<span class=\"text-[12px] font-normal\">/yr once running</span>', and append a total row: 'Together, once running: about $1.2M a year (overlap removed)'.\n- Make roi.html open on the same three plays (inPlan true only for 1, 4 and 5). If the five-play plan stays, rename its hub label from 'The plan, each sale counted once' to 'If you run five of the seven' and name the five.",
